cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Donghyuncop (동현콥): a one-button flight laboratory that runs a classic Flash helicopter game unmodified and sets its speed through the esoteric language Donghyun-lang"
type: software
version: "0.1"
date-released: "2026-10-29"
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Dong Hyun
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9883-0229"
    affiliation: "Inha University College of Medicine"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Raspberry-Kim/donghyun-lab5"
url: "https://raspberry-kim.github.io/donghyun-lab5/"
abstract: >-
  Donghyuncop is a browser-based, noncommercial one-button flight laboratory.
  It plays the classic Flash "Helicopter Game" (SeeThru.co.uk; design David
  McCandless, Flash Leandro Barreto) from the original SWF file, byte for byte
  unmodified and verified by SHA-256 at every load, through the Ruffle
  emulator. The only control is the left mouse button or a touch on the game
  screen. The only setting, the helicopter speed (50-200 percent, 100 being
  the original 30 frames per second), is chosen through a program written in
  the esoteric programming language Donghyun-lang. A small generated wrapper
  SWF loads the original into _level1, sets the frame rate, and works around
  a Ruffle frame-ordering issue without changing the original. The MIT
  license applies to the Donghyuncop code and documentation only; the
  original SWF remains the property of its authors and is not covered by it.
  Ruffle is under MIT or Apache-2.0 and the fonts under the SIL Open Font
  License. See LICENSE and CREDITS.md.
keywords:
  - Flash
  - Ruffle
  - game preservation
  - one-button game
  - esoteric programming language
  - JavaScript
